\f1\fs22 As the conversation unfolded, it became clear the Sages were foreign agents, possibly for the Greeks or Russians or the Woke Democracy of All-Access Wrestling. Alexander became convinced they had not only  infiltrated whatever this Project Kebab was\'97for which Sarah was the pretty face, and some guy called Johnny was the ceremonial head\'97the Sages were running it every step of the way. They were feeding this Johnny ideas,  which he called his own. Alexander knew the type; they infested the infotainment industry.\
Beneath it all, the Sages clearly had more than a weird-uncle interest in his and Sarah\'92s baby\'97Little Clinton, these traitors were calling him. He\'92d be called Alexander Lysander Ulysses Shakti, if Alexander had anything to do with it. \
And Alexander had everything to do with it. He swore he\'92d protect Alex Junior from anyone who thought they owned a piece of him\'97the Sages, the Elvi, his own mother, even Chanta.\
What could Chanta possibly have to do with any of this? He was just a cleaner. Alexander could buy him dozens of times over. He\'92d already bought him dozens of times over, throwing him the messiest crime scenes that no one else wanted or asked too many questions about.\
Chanta was a friend. He\'92d been moderately useful for years. But if he thinks he\'92s going to be at the birth, Alexander would clean any notion of that out of his head.\
Alexander\'92s mood soured when they mentioned his mother. 
\f3\i Eloise is on Eloise\'92s side
\f1\i0 , one of them said. He was right about that. At the very moment Alexander had everything he wanted, his mother had exiled him from it. Falsely. For a sham job at a sham company. How long did she think he\'92d be fooled?\
Not long enough. That was the answer to 
\f3\i that
\f1\i0  question. He was back, and realising just how many spells Eloise had been casting. She cast a spell over the Elvi and wicked Sarah away from him once before, and then denied him his dreams-come-true on the night of their Holy Joint Venture. He knew Sarah wanted to be with him always, and his mother had denied them both.\
What ever Project Kebab was, Alexander knew enough to know that once a son-exiling arms dealer, always a son-exiling arms dealer. When the Sages mentioned her engineers\'97complimented them, it sounded like\'97He knew exactly what she was doing: she was building a weapon. A weapon that would secure her power over him and deny him from ever being happy.\
Not a thing she could pull a trigger on and blast him to despair. Alexander knew his mother\'92s weapons could be as subtle as a friendly letter. It was more a plan to invent a project to build a weapon that kept him and Sarah apart. That was the weapon.\
And the Sages bought it too. They were as blind as anyone\'97even dare he say it?\'97the woman he knew he would cherish in pictures on his arm for the rest of his life.\
Sarah had been fooled too.\
Perhaps he should divorce her. What\'92s the point of possessing a beautiful woman if you couldn\'92t discard her too?\
One thing he knew for sure: there was a film treatment in there somehow.\
But Gold Budgies and Best Producer/Writer/Actor awards would have to wait.\
If Alexander had worked himself into righteous fury over his mother\'92s mistreatment, that paled when the Sages mentioned him\'97
\f3\i him
\f1\i0 , personally\'97and then laugh.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

